{
  "title": "Namaz for Fulfillment of Needs (4)",
  "data": "Upon concluding the prayer, say the following supplication:\nيَا كَرِيْمُ يَا كَرِيْمُ يَا كَرِيْمُ\nYAA KAREEMU YAA KAREEMU YAA KAREEM\nO Generous! O Generous! O Generous!\nيَا عَظِيْمُ يَا عَظِيْمُ يَا عَظِيْمُ\nYAA A'ZEEMU YAA A'ZEEMU YAA A'ZEEM\nO Great! O Great! O Great!\nيَا اَعْظَمَ مِنْ كُلِّ عَظِيْمٍ\nYAA A'ZAMA MIN KULLI A'ZEEM\nO He Who is greater than every great one!\nيَا سَمِيْعَ الدُّعَآءِ\nYAA SAMEE'AD DU'AA'\nO Hearer of prayer!\nيَا مَنْ لَا تُغَيِّرُهُ اللَّيَالِيْ وَالْاَيَّامُ\nYAA MAN LAA TUGHAYYIRUHUL LAYAALEE WAL AYYAAM\nO He Whom the nights and the days do not change!\nصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّاٰلِهٖ\nSALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIH\nSend blessings upon Muhammad and his Household,\nوَارْحَمْ ضَعْفِيْ وَفَقْرِيْ وَفَاقَتِيْ وَمَسْكَنَتِيْ\nWARHAM DA'FEE WA FAQREE WA FAAQATEE WA MASKANATEE\nand have mercy on my weakness, my poverty, my want and my lowliness,\nفَاِنَّكَ اَعْلَمُ بِهَا مِنِّيْ\nFA-INNAKA A'LAMU BIHAA MINNEE\nfor You know them better than I do,\nوَاَنْتَ اَعْلَمُ بِحَاجَتِيْ\nWA ANTA A'LAMU BIHAAJATEE\nand You know my need best.\nيَا مَنْ رَحِمَ الشَّيْخَ يَعْقُوْبَ\nYAA MAN RAHIMASH SHAYKHA YA'QOOB\nO He Who had mercy on the aged Jacob\nحِيْنَ رَدَّ عَلَيْهِ يُوْسُفَ قُرَّةَ عَيْنِهٖ\nHEENA RADDA A'LAYHI YOOSUFA QURRATA A'YNIH\nwhen He restored Joseph, the delight of his eye, to him!\nيَا مَنْ رَحِمَ اَيُّوْبَ بَعْدَ طُوْلِ بَلَآئِهٖ\nYAA MAN RAHIMA AYYOOBA BA'DA TOOLI BALAA'IH\nO He Who had mercy on Job after his long affliction!\nيَا مَنْ رَحِمَ مُحَمَّدًا\nYAA MAN RAHIMA MUHAMMADAN\nO He Who had mercy on Muhammad,\nوَّمِنَ الْيُتْمِ اٰوَاهُ\nWA MINAL YUTMI AAWAAH\ngave him shelter in his orphanhood,\nوَنَصَرَهٗ عَلٰى جَبَابِرَةِ قُرَيْشٍ وَطَوَاغِيْتِهَا\nWA NASARAHOO A'LAA JABAABIRATI QURAYSHIN WA TAWAAGHEETIHAA\ngranted him victory over the tyrants and false idols of Quraysh,\nوَاَمْكَنَهٗ مِنْهُمْ\nWA AMKANAHOO MINHUM\nand gave him power over them!\nيَا مُغِيْثُ يَا مُغِيْثُ يَا مُغِيْثُ\nYAA MUGHEETHU YAA MUGHEETHU YAA MUGHEETH\nO Helper! O Helper! O Helper!\nRepeat this last phrase many times, and then ask Almighty Allah for your need, for He will grant it.",
  "merits": "It is reported that one who has a request to be granted by Almighty Allah may offer a four-unit prayer, reciting [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) and [Surah al-An'am](A10) in each unit."
}
